1. d4 d5 {"A notable absentee when play began this morning was Rubinstein, who
did not arrive until his clock had been going for thirty-five minutes. A
messenger to his hotel found him in bed under the impression his watch was an
hour fast. Fortunately for Rubinstein, Norman made a positional error early in
the game, or Rubinstein might have found the clock and his opponent too
danger­ous a combination." (The Times, 29 December 1922)} 2. Nf3 e6 3. c4 a6
